<p>A South Korean appeals court on Thursday reduced former Prime Minister Han Duck-soo’s prison sentence from 23 years to 15 years while upholding his conviction over his role in former President Yoon Suk Yeol’s brief imposition of martial law in December 2024. A Seoul High Court panel led by Judge Lee Seung-cheol issued the decision, The Korea Times reported.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/I2M8oMXHFIFZ5kIms7K0cvC2LKDJ-hvegnmnHukHsqRM7Q4PBvL24HmLOMPMSqeuHjRarvmvSrpDyo3tBu_7DE1mKc5T1DnN7DmgA1ALunpFNupWfwrUg-2ehLni-uWFaQrM7tKq_lH9ooZiW77Qs8danmxXj1AwZCYFV8_2sSPOO2czuLUEJFD20Xp7Vp-sRrfVglEW_vV7_FyjYYdYbLktQjblQ2TSfg_z7nxCls_p6Fz-TL80wDP7MrJy4NTQ13dd' alt='Former South Korean Prime Minister Han Duck-soo, whose prison sentence was reduced to 15 years on appeal.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Evidence finding: No Cut News reported that judges said Han received Yoon’s public address and martial-law proclamation documents before the declaration, which they said showed he could understand an alleged plan to block National Assembly functions.</li><li>Additional conduct: No Cut News reported that the court also cited Han’s involvement in discussions about cutting electricity and water to specific media outlets.</li><li>Basis for sentence: Czech outlet Seznam Zprávy reported that the court took Han’s long public service into account when it reduced the term by eight years.</li><li>Prosecution appeal: No Cut News reported that the court rejected the special prosecutor’s appeal over an allegation involving the use of falsely prepared official documents.</li></ul><blockquote>Never be tolerated under any circumstances - Seoul High Court panel</blockquote><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Seoul High Court: The court said Han played an important role by proposing a Cabinet meeting that made the martial law decision appear to have gone through proper deliberation. (<a href='https://www.koreatimes.co.kr/southkorea/law-crime/20260507/appeals-court-cuts-ex-pms-sentence-to-15-years-but-upholds-insurrection-conviction'>The Korea Times</a>)</li><li>Han Duck-soo: Han denies guilt and says he did not support the martial law declaration. (<a href='https://www.idnes.cz/zpravy/zahranicni/jihokorejsky-expremier-stanne-pravo-soud-trest.A260507_061227_zahranicni_kurl#utm_source=rss&amp;utm_medium=feed&amp;utm_campaign=zpravodaj&amp;utm_content=main'>iDNES.cz</a>)</li><li>Han Duck-soo’s lawyer: The defense lawyer said Han would appeal again after the Seoul appeals court reduced, but did not overturn, his prison term. (<a href='https://www.dw.com/ru/в-южной-корее-апелляционный-суд-сократил-срок-экс-премьеру-хан-док-су/a-77073107'>Deutsche Welle</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://abcnews.com/International/wireStory/south-korean-court-reduces-prison-sentence-prime-minister-132734163'>South Korean court reduces prison sentence for ex-prime minister in martial law case</a> - abcnews.com</li><li><a href='https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/5/7/south-korean-court-reduces-han-duck-soos-prison-term-in-martial-law-case'>South Korean court reduces Han Duck-soo’s prison term in martial law case</a> - aljazeera.com</li><li><a href='https://www.scmp.com/news/asia/east-asia/article/3352689/south-korean-court-cuts-former-prime-minister-han-duck-soos-jail-term-15-years'>South Korean court cuts former prime minister Han Duck-soo’s jail term to 15 years</a> - scmp.com</li><li><a href='https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/south-korean-court-reduces-prison-sentence-for-former-prime-minister-in-martial-law-case/article70949769.ece'>South Korean court reduces prison sentence for former Prime Minister in martial law case</a> - thehindu.com</li><li><a href='https://www.straitstimes.com/asia/south-korea-appeals-court-cuts-jail-term-for-ex-pm-han-to-15-years-in-martial-law-case'>South Korea appeals court cuts jail term for ex-PM Han to 15 years in martial law case</a> - straitstimes.com</li><li><a href='https://www.asiaone.com/asia/south-korea-appea